# Moxa ioThinx 45MR-4420.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioThinx 45MR-4420 — 4-channel AO (analog output)
# | 
# | Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP via ioThinx 4510 adapter, port 502
# | 
# | IMPORTANT: Addresses are MODULE-RELATIVE. Actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address.
# | Slot base depends on which slot this module occupies in the ioThinx 4510 chassis.
# | 
# | FC03 (holding R/W): see [[registers]] below
# | FC04 (input R): aoMode ch0-3 (4 WORD, 0=disable 1=0-10V 2=0-20mA 3=4-20mA 4=±10V)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioThinx 45MR-4420
@description=4-AO analog output ioThinx 45MR slot module. Addresses are module-relative; actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address. FC03: aoValueRaw ch0-3 (raw DAC counts, rel 0-3), aoValueScaled ch0-3 (f32 engineering-unit value, 2 regs/ch = 8 regs, rel 4-11). FC04: aoMode ch0-3 (0=disable 1=0-10V 2=0-20mA 3=4-20mA 4=±10V). Write to aoValueScaled to set output in engineering units; write to aoValueRaw for raw DAC counts.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iothinx-45mr-4420.toml; Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
